Like that's to be expected.

00:34:04.020 --> 00:34:08.720
But what I'm talking about is mostly what you were talking about in the, just the general sense of that.

00:34:08.720 --> 00:34:16.080
There's certainly enough variety between all of the different types of units you have to command the different, uh, types of terrain you'll be at.

00:34:16.220 --> 00:34:23.780
And the, uh, even though the goal always remains the same, uh, there is something here for the player who finds it interesting.

00:34:23.780 --> 00:34:36.760
And I think that's the next question is, uh, you know, mostly at this time with the exception of maybe a hardcore devoted few, uh, the NES is seen as a video game console for kids.

00:34:36.760 --> 00:34:50.160
And I can't help but feel like, um, not that no kids would like this, but that this is more of the kind of game that, uh, dad secretly like finds out or gets, you know, for Christmas or something like, oh, you play two or whatever.

00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:55.780
And then dad gets obsessed with it because he can actually understand the strategy side of things.

